      "problem": "Find the inverse of $f(x) = 3x - 4.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow the four steps below.\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y.$\n\n$$\ny = 3x-4\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y.$\n\n$$\nx = 3y-4\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3y-4 \\\\ x+4 & =3y \\\\ \\frac{x+4}{3} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x).$\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac {x + 4} {3}\n$$",
